# This file becomes the root .gitattributes of this skill's split/<name> branch.
#
# install.sh clones split/<name> for a normal install, and `git subtree split
# --prefix=skills/<name>` carries only this directory — the monorepo's root
# .gitattributes never reaches that branch. Without this copy, a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) rewrites every file here to CRLF.
# That is harmless under Git Bash, which tolerates \r, but it breaks the scripts the
# moment they run anywhere stricter: a shebang becomes "/usr/bin/env bash\r" under
# WSL, Linux, or macOS, and direct execution of .py and .mjs entry points fails the
# same way. Skills are executed by whichever agent and shell the user runs, so the
# checkout must not depend on who cloned it.
#
# Keep this identical to the monorepo root .gitattributes; tests/validate-skill-evals.py
# enforces that.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch interpreters require CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
